  "scenario": "A global online marketplace runs flash sales attracting more than 500,000 concurrent buyers competing for limited-edition product drops. Product catalog data — listings, pricing, and stock positions — is read tens of millions of times per hour during a sale, while inventory must remain consistent across regional warehouses to prevent overselling.\n\nDuring a Black Friday flash sale, product catalog reads became a latency bottleneck under surge traffic. DynamoDB read throttling caused stale availability data to be served for 22 minutes, resulting in 38,000 oversold items across 12 product lines, $1.9M in fulfilment losses, and a logistics partner penalty for missed dispatch SLAs.\n\nThe outgoing engineering team has left behind a complete, containerized Java Spring Boot Order API. The application is fully implemented, with the Amazon DAX client already integrated, but the supporting AWS services have not yet been deployed, configured, or integrated.\n\nYour responsibility is to deploy the application, configure the required AWS services, integrate them, and validate the complete order placement and fulfilment workflow.",
